	\L_02572:
	\L_02556:
	ZH 1:
	'　Planned City Laurengrad'
	R
	R
	'  2nd Army HQ - Rear Garden'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'2nd Army General Aristoles was'
	R
	'in the beautifully maintained'
	R
	'garden, lost in thought.'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0253a:
	ZH 1:
	'War with Leazas...?'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'...Patton...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'It was years ago...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'My friend took down Leazas, then'
	R
	'got counterattacked and went'
	R
	'missing...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Ridiculous... I gave up back'
	R
	'then, but this stinks of'
	R
	'conspiracy...'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_02556:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles looked up at the'
	R
	'deep blue sky.'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0253a:
	ZH 1:
	'............'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Empress Sheila... Are the'
	R
	'rumors that you hate him true?'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'You,'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'who always looked at your'
	R
	'brother-in-law Patton with worry'
	R
	'at banquets and so many public'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'gatherings...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'I don’t want to believe you'
	R
	'would give orders to have'
	R
	'Patton killed...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Dowager Empress Pamela and that'
	R
	'pale man... Stessel...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'are likely pulling the strings,'
	R
	'but...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'I’ve yet to even get proof of'
	R
	'that. If I could just get some'
	R
	'somehow...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'I keep sending out spies to get'
	R
	'any...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'But I still haven’t obtained any'
	R
	'significant information...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Impressive, Stessel... You may'
	R
	'be an enemy, but I acknowledge'
	R
	'your intelligence...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'I can’t respect you, though...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'If Pamela and Stessel are found'
	R
	'as the puppet masters, maybe'
	R
	'banishment, or...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'They likely can’t escape'
	R
	'execution.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'And then... Empress Sheila will'
	R
	'be left, and I should be able to'
	R
	'protect her if I take her in.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Then... In the off chance that'
	R
	'Patton happens to be alive and'
	R
	'he returns to this country...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'I want to believe everything'
	R
	'will go well...'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_02556:
	ZH 1:
	'The opportunity for Patton and'
	R
	'Aristoles to meet was given by'
	R
	'Thoma, who was now dead.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles was twelve back then.'
	R
	'Patton was ten.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles was already treated as'
	R
	'a prodigy, and received respect,'
	R
	'fear,'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'and jealousy as a crossbow'
	R
	'master.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'At a time when he was'
	R
	'overwhelmed by trying to be'
	R
	'perfect at everything,'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'he met Thoma, and then...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Thoma had said he wanted to'
	R
	'introduce him to someone,'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'so he followed passively to meet'
	R
	'Patton, rude but training hard.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Their personalities and'
	R
	'characters were complete'
	R
	'opposites.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'But, perhaps because of that,'
	R
	'they became friends in no time'
	R
	'at all.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'That was 20 years ago.'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0253a:
	ZH 1:
	'Patton...'
	R
	'Where are you now and what are'
	R
	'you doing?'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Are you really dead like the'
	R
	'rumors say? Do you live?'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0258e:
	ZH 1:
	'Aaaaaagh, geez!'
	R
	'What’re you doin’ here,'
	R
	'General Aristoles!?'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	!VAR0516 : 433!
	\L_025e2:
	\L_025c6:
	ZH 1:
	'The fat man that ran like he was'
	R
	'dragging himself was Aristoles’s'
	R
	'subordinate, Convert Tax.'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0258e:
	ZH 1:
	'What’re you loiterin’ around'
	R
	'here for?!'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'We’re at war!'
	R
	'Mr. Stessel’s gonna yell at us'
	R
	'if we don’t go out and fight.'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0251e:
	ZH 1:
	'............'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Hmph... What do I care? I have'
	R
	'no intention of fighting for'
	R
	'him.'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_025aa:
	ZH 1:
	'...Ack... That was a mistake.'
	R
	'Can’t say Mr. Stessel’s name'
	R
	'around this guy.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Since he suspects it was Mr.'
	R
	'Stessel that drove Prince'
	R
	'Patton out...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Well, guess anyone’d feel bad'
	R
	'if their good friend was'
	R
	'killed...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Can’t say that, though.'
	R
	'Mr. Stessel told me to use'
	R
	'him...'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0258e:
	ZH 1:
	'Aah, right.'
	R
	'On a different subject...'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0251e:
	ZH 1:
	'What?'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0258e:
	ZH 1:
	'A letter came for you from'
	R
	'Empress Sheila. Look.'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0251e:
	ZH 1:
	'What!?'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_02556:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles snatched the letter'
	R
	'from Convert’s hands.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'  To my beloved Aristoles.'
	R
	'  How are you?'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'As I live like a caged bird   in'
	R
	'this castle,'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'I can only   know what you’re'
	R
	'doing via   reports on paper.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'I’m lonely. While their   army’s'
	R
	'not as great as ours,   the'
	R
	'Leazas Army is strong...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'I believe they’re a problem.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'  But Aristoles...   For our'
	R
	'citizens who are   forced to'
	R
	'live lives of   poverty...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'　　And for me, please fight...'
	R
	'  Please protect us...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'  I will be sincerely waiting'
	R
	'for reports from you in the'
	R
	'castle.             Sheila'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0251e:
	ZH 1:
	'Empress Sheila...'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_02556:
	ZH 1:
	'Aristoles hugged the letter'
	R
	'against his chest like he was'
	R
	'in love with it.'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0258e:
	ZH 1:
	'What’d it say?'
	R
	'A letter directly from Empress'
	R
	'Sheila...'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0251e:
	ZH 1:
	'Don’t touch it.'
	R
	'This letter was written for me'
	R
	'alone.'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Nobody else can look at it, or'
	R
	'even touch it.'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0258e:
	ZH 1:
	'Huh... Sorry...'
	\L_02643:
	\L_02636:
	\L_0253a:
	ZH 1:
	'Empress Sheila...'
	\L_02643:
	ZH 1:
	'Yes... The reason I stay in this'
	R
	'country isn’t for the people,'
